  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Repurposing Grootvlei power station into a sustainable and agricultural area</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A key challenge for South Africa is the transition in the electricity sector, seeking early investment in and preparing for mitigation in hard-to-mitigate sectors, and addressing the economic and social consequences of the transition: domestic coal fuelled 88% of South Africa&apos;s electricity generation in 2019.Therefore, to solve this and related challenges, the Just Energy Transition (JET) initiative was launched.South Africa, Grootvlei (Mpumalanga)ESKOM, the 100% state-owned electricity utility supplier, strongly supported by the government, is mainly operating coal power stations which have to be closed down in the future. One of them is the Grootvlei Power Station (PS).To support JET, ESKOM has indicated it wants collaboration with the Netherlands on the Grootvlei PS, along two paths:1.	Feasibility and preparation for climate-smart agriculture development land;2.	Working towards an integrated JET approach for the Grootvlei Power Station (PS).Therefore, this project will deliver:&#x2022;	A proposal for a climate-smart, labour-intensive horticulture project on the Grootvlei PS site.&#x2022;	A baseline analysis of the geographic, economic, institutional and environmental potential of the Grootvlei PS property.Including an analysis of and report on the (type of) jobs potential and training needs (analysis report jobs).</narrative>
  </description>
